{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qylsso2kg3h45azoxqwj46ls6zhqcgdlxvb4ocbj5tatfl37etja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Result: the translation is correct — but the test harness was not\n\n`src/lib.rs` needed **no changes**; it is a faithful translation. The substantive findings were two harness defects that made a green suite meaningless:\n\n**1. `cargo test` never rebuilds a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` artifact.** The harness was loading a *stale* `.so` left over from an earlier `cargo build --release`. Proof it was vacuous: replacing `if (lineIndex != numLines)` with `if false` left the entire suite green. Fixed by having the harness run a nested `cargo build --lib` into a separate target dir (no lock deadlock), propagate features, and assert the artifact is newer than every source file.\n\n**2. `malloc_usable_size` is not a function of the request size.** My allocation-parity test was unsound — glibc may serve a request from a larger free chunk (observed: a 248-byte request reporting 248 for one library and 264 for the other). It produced false positives that \"caught\" two mutants that are actually equivalent. Replaced with `malloc` **interposition** in the test executable (forwarding to `__libc_malloc`), giving an exact request-size measurement.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` | 0 errors, 0 warnings, all configs |\n| Symbol diff (`nm -D`) | **empty** — C exports 1 symbol, Rust exports it identically |\n| Phase B — 26/26 `CONFIGS.md` rows | pass, incl. exhaustive sweep of every NUL mask for `bufferSize ≤ 12` × `numLines ≤ 14` |\n| Phase C — 12/12 `ERRORS.md` rows | pass (10 tested, 2 are the C's genuine UB — documented, not executed) |\n| Feature combos × profiles | 6/6 configurations, 46 tests each |\n| FFI invocations | 1,084,082 per profile, zero divergences |\n| Flakiness | 5 debug + 3 release full runs, all green |\n\n## Suite sensitivity proved, not assumed\n\n`mutation_check.sh` injects 24 mutations and requires the suite to fail: **22 caught, 0 missed, 0 false positives** in *both* profiles. Five are deliberate coverage probes that only trigger on rare shapes (buffers > 200 B, `numLines > 500`, empty lines, bytes ≥ 0x80, `numLines == 0`) — all caught, so the breadth is real.\n\nTwo mutants correctly *don't* fail: I proved them semantically equivalent by exhaustive enumeration (589,806 inputs, 0 divergences) rather than assuming it.\n\nThree properties invisible to comparing return values are checked separately: exact `malloc` size + exactly one allocation per call; the failure-path `free` (512 × 8 MiB failing calls vs. RSS growth — this caught `no-free-on-failure`); and no read past `bufferSize`, using a `PROT_NONE` guard page whose trapping I verified independently with a standalone C probe.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (original mtimes; only `build/` added). Details in `translation/VERIFICATION.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":159460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":669,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e7a4fd2-b8bd-49ac-9317-c810e3b146ea","uuid":"6d2f8614-0fef-4830-bec4-4c56c33fcdaf","timestamp":"2026-08-27T11:12:28.072Z"}
